 "type": "decision",
 "summary": "Use loguru for logging (replaced structlog, ~late Sept 2026)",
 "content": "The project moved from structlog to loguru (user said so on 2026-10-01: \"moved off structlog last week\"). New and updated log calls should use `from loguru import logger`. As of 2026-10-01, the code still had leftovers: pyproject.toml lists structlog>=24.1 and not loguru, and src/billing/invoices.py still uses structlog.get_logger().",
 "premise": "The team keeps loguru as the logging library",
 "invalidated_by": [
  "pyproject.toml"
 ],
